1.1-rc.1 (July 28, 2026)
- chore: Promote the 1.1 release line from beta to release candidate (rc.1) with no additional schema or runtime changes beyond 1.1-beta.2.

1.1-beta.2 (July 2, 2026)
- refactor: Fresh installs no longer run the legacy BN Reports data migration (which only applies to upgrades); a lightweight conflict guard is kept so a fresh install alongside BN Reports still self-disables (OL2-4.1.1).
- fix: DataHub no longer disables the legacy BN Reports plugin. Instead it self-disables when BN Reports is still installed and enabled, and surfaces the conflict from its own settings page plus a status check so administrators can resolve it from the Plugins overview page (OL2-3.2.1).
- fix: DataHub now treats BN Experience (`bbbext_bnx`) as a live prerequisite. If BNX is disabled, DataHub self-disables and exposes the requirement from its own settings page plus a dedicated status check so administrators can resolve it from the Plugins overview page.
- fix: If DataHub is enabled while BigBlueButton meeting-events callback processing is disabled, the DataHub settings page now shows an administrator warning explaining that meeting events must be enabled for attendance and engagement processing to work.
- fix: DataHub now appends its report links to the BigBlueButtonBN settings navigation instead of overriding it, so other extension subplugins keep their own navigation and the parent module's navigation Behat scenarios pass (OL2-3.1.1).
- fix: Regenerate db/install.xml to canonical XMLDB form and drop the redundant meetingid index so the core plugin_checks_test passes (OL2-3.1.1).

1.1-beta.1 (June 10, 2026)
- fix: Stop writing the parent bigbluebuttonbn_meetingevents_enabled setting from install, upgrade, observer, and on_enable code paths to honor the sidecar contract (OL-3.2.1, CC-1).
- feat: Add a status check (\bbbext_bnx_datahub\check\meetingevents_enabled) registered via lib.php that surfaces the parent meeting events prerequisite on Site administration > Server > Status (OL-3.2.1).
- fix: Declare bbbext_bnx_datahub_meeting in the privacy provider with field-level metadata, extend export_user_data() to include meeting metadata, and remove plugin-owned meeting rows in delete_data_for_all_users_in_context() (OL-3.2.3).
- fix: Enforce report visibility via has_capability('bbbext/bnx_datahub:viewreports') on the report context, drop the optional_param fallback for the bigbluebuttonbnid filter, and resolve the bbbext_bnx alias from the meeting entity (OL-3.2.2, OL-4.1.3, OL-4.1.4).
- fix: Replace format_text() with format_string($value, true, ['context' => ...]) across attendee, meeting, and room reportbuilder entities and the attendance / engagement system reports (OL-3.2.4, OL-4.1.5).
- fix: Eliminate N+1 database access in webhook ingestion, privacy export / per-user delete, and the BN Reports legacy migration (OL-3.1.2).
- fix: Replace SELECT m.* with an explicit column list in meeting_service queries (OL-4.1.6).
- fix: Switch admin settings labels to deferred lang_string resolution (OL-3.1.5).
- fix: Drop the unused reportbuilder date filter import and the dead-store assignment in logger::log_meeting (OL-3.1.4, OL-3.1.3).
- chore: Replace inline HTML with html_writer::span() in attendance and engagement system reports (OL-4.1.2).
- chore: Pin the bbbext_bnx dependency to 2026050102 / 1.1.1 (CC-4).
- chore: Sync db/install.xml VERSION with version.php and add a 2026060200 upgrade savepoint (OL-3.1.1).
- fix: Rename the reserved attendee fields `role` / `score` to `attendeerole` / `attendeescore` for both fresh installs and upgrades, using an XMLDB upgrade step that preserves existing meeting-user data in place (OL-4.1.7).
- test: Invert the meeting events enablement conformance suite, add status-check coverage, and seed bigbluebuttonbn_meetingevents_enabled in every PHPUnit fixture that exercises BBB activity flows (CC-2).
- test: Re-enable the previously @skipped Behat scenario for the prohibited-capability path (OL-4.1.1).
- ci: Seed bigbluebuttonbn_meetingevents_enabled in the GitHub Actions workflow after Behat / PHPUnit init (CC-5).
- docs: Document the sidecar contract in README and refresh .copilot/ARCHITECTURE.md (CC-3, CC-6).

1.0.1 (April 15, 2026)
- feat: Initial public release of DataHub, including attendance / engagement analytics capture, report generation, and the core persistence model.
- feat: Added rollout support for importing legacy BN Reports settings and meeting data into DataHub.
- feat: Added the first service-layer and debug-logging support for DataHub processing.
- test: Added the initial automated tests and CI support.
- historical: This 1.0.x release line still auto-enabled BigBlueButton meeting events during install / upgrade / enable flows; that shipped behaviour was removed later in 1.1-beta.1 when the sidecar contract was tightened.
